# @projexlight scope: Verdaccio in dev, npm.projexcloud.com in prod.
#
# This ONE line decides where `pnpm publish` and `pnpm install` go for the scope.
# Packages deliberately do NOT set publishConfig.registry: npm resolves the publish target
# as publishConfig.registry > .npmrc scope registry > default, so a value baked into a
# package.json WINS over anything CI sets, and a production release would then quietly
# publish to a developer's laptop and report success. Keeping the registry here, and only
# here, is what lets dev and production differ at all.
#
# Switch without editing this file:
#   node scripts/release/set-registry.js prod     # prints the exported env for CI
#   npm_config_@projexlight:registry=https://npm.projexcloud.com/ pnpm publish -r
#
# Auth tokens are NEVER committed. Configure via one of:
#   1. User-level npm config: npm config set //localhost:4873/:_authToken=<token>
#   2. CI env: NPM_TOKEN=... (release.yml passes this through to npm publish)
@projexlight:registry=http://localhost:4873/
